/**
 * Natur & geografi → Växter & svampar → Trädgård & odling, 2851–2857 (0.45): sowing and planting, watering and
 * fertilising, soil and compost, pruning and thinning, pests and plant diseases, harvest and storage, and growing on
 * a balcony.
 * Recurring signs: a brown cut of soil below the ground line (y = 112) when roots, seeds or bulbs matter; terracotta
 * pots; the thing the word names ringed in orange; movement and change shown with orange arrows; water as blue
 * drops. Abstract words and adjectives are small symbolic scenes where the coloured idea dominates and a grey copy
 * stands beside it as contrast. Digits only; no words, no brands and no pointing fingers.
 */
